1
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:24,300
Those with no money, come to my place.

2
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:29,020
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky and white clouds.

4
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:36,420
Eyes

5
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:42,940
Somehow it'll all work out, I'm sure.

6
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,900
Those without work, come to my place.

7
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

8
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:12,100
Look at the steel masses burning.

9
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:18,260
Somehow it'll all work out, I'm sure.

10
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

11
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,480
If you get it, gather up and follow me.

12
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,700
Decision Ranking King

13
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,700
Hurry up, Ryo-chan.

14
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:53,840
We're spending all our money on this,
so let me take my time choosing.

15
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:56,160
All our money is just a little over 100 yen,
you know.

16
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,460
That's because you're always wasting money.

17
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:01,420
That's exactly why I'm trying to
spend it carefully this time, dammit.

18
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:02,440
Yeah, yeah.

19
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,400
Should I go with the
classic Cup Noodle, then?

20
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,640
No, the ramen shop one
is hard to pass up, too.

21
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:13,280
And now, the announcement of the
number one cup ramen on our ranking.

22
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:16,960
What is this show?

23
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:19,600
It's Mister Ranking.
It's actually pretty popular.

24
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:23,500
Products that reach number one
on this show sell out in no time.

25
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:29,520
The cup ramen I, the one who decides the top spot,
recommend for first place is this one.

26
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:32,560
Kusaya Natto Ramen, Blue Cheese Flavor

27
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:37,540
Come on, you too, go ahead and taste
it with your own tongue right now.

28
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:42,120
Hyottoko Foods' Kusaya Natto Ramen,
Blue Cheese Flavor

29
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:45,780
Kusaya Natto Ramen, Blue Cheese Flavor.
Found it!

30
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,300
Alright, it's done!

31
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:54,200
Looks tasty.

32
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,820
Doesn't it smell weird somehow?

33
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,720
And the soup's color is kind of creepy, too.

34
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,540
Doesn't look very tasty, does it?

35
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:03,100
What are you talking about?
It's the number one ranked ramen!

36
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,440
It can't possibly be bad.

37
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,220
Itadakimasu.

38
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:11,620
No way.

39
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:16,320
Ryo-san can't even eat it?

40
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:18,500
It must taste really awful.

41
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,800
What a terrible experience.

42
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,620
Why would something like
that be ranked first?

43
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:24,640
What's wrong, Sakonji?

44
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:25,880
I... I've been tricked.

45
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,480
Actually, on last week's Mr. Ranking...

46
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:35,980
Regional General News 1! Beautiful girl figures,
that's what this is all about!

47
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:38,660
A Saori figure, popular among certain fans!

48
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:39,320
What!?

49
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:42,840
This kind of product is out there!

50
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:49,000
I searched high and low for it,

51
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,820
and today I finally got my hands on it.

52
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:56,500
It's a big package, isn't it.

53
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:57,840
Here it is.

54
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:01,040
So this is Saori?

55
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:04,040
It looks like Golgo 13 after a weeding!

56
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,940
And on top of that, it's huge.

57
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:09,060
I thought it was half-size,

58
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:10,900
but it turned out to be double size!

59
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:13,100
This isn't it!

60
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:17,340
Here's another victim of Mr. Ranking.

61
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:20,460
Reiko, is that ranking really accurate?

62
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,280
That's what Komachi and
the others said, though.

63
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,640
Those guys

64
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:28,084
Komachi,

65
00:04:28,134 --> 00:04:31,880
Naoko! I need to ask you about Mr. Ranking!

66
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,720
R-Ryotsu Kankichi.

67
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:36,240
Mr. Ranking? What about it?

68
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:40,120
Hearing that name right now
puts me in a really bad mood.

69
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,900
W-what happened?

70
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:44,560
You're giving it to me?

71
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:45,920
Try it.

72
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,780
What's that? Is that some kind of game food?

73
00:04:59,260 --> 00:05:02,940
It's the chocolate that was ranked
number one on Mr. Ranking a while back.

74
00:05:02,940 --> 00:05:05,100
And we went through so
much trouble to get it.

75
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:09,040
You're the one who said that
ranking was trustworthy, right?

76
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:14,080
We trusted that ranking
and got burned for it.

77
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,100
Yeah, that's right.

78
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:20,220
It's true, when the show first started,
the rankings were pretty reliable.

79
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:21,620
Y-yeah, that's right.

80
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:24,200
But lately they've been wrong a lot.

81
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,360
Yeah, exactly.

82
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,240
I'm never going to believe a word the
Number One Decider statue says again.

83
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,700
Decide the number one!

84
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:34,360
That old man who makes the rankings.

85
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:37,900
So if you've got complaints, take them
up with the Number One Decider statue.

86
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:38,940
Take them up with him, got it?

87
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:46,760
This is it, alright, let's go.

88
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:48,660
Well then, thanks.

89
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,280
Sorry.

90
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,200
Watch yourself.

91
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:51,700
Yes.

92
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,240
What's so funny?

93
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,020
Excuse me.

94
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:02,360
I never expected such a
off-base lecture to come along.

95
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,900
How is it off-base?

96
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:06,440
I'm just saying bad food is bad.

97
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:10,620
Do you know what happened when
Coca-Cola was first imported?

98
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:11,520
See?

99
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:14,740
Many Japanese people said it tasted weird.

100
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:17,980
They avoided it,
saying it wasn't fit for human consumption.

101
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,760
But now, how is it?

102
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:22,800
Now it's loved by almost
all Japanese people.

103
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:29,520
Are you trying to say the same
goes for Kusaya natto ramen?

104
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,220
My ranking looks even into the future.

105
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:37,280
Excuse me, but your sense of
taste must be quite outdated.

106
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:40,860
Well then, what about the
figures people buy these days?

107
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:47,360
This isn't a matter of
taste or anything like that.

108
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,760
It's just a weird face.

109
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:53,280
Come on,
you just happened to get a defective one.

110
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,360
How unfortunate.

111
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,960
I thought the same thing, so I...

112
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,780
I bought one too, you know!

113
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:01,300
Where's the Saori in this?

114
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:05,060
You're really unlucky too.

115
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:07,400
Getting defective ones every single time.

116
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:08,940
Hey, is it about to come off already?

117
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:12,580
I'm running late.

118
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:16,560
I have an appointment with someone,
so I'm sorry, but

119
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,760
Please leave.

120
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:18,860
See you later.

121
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,920
This guy seems pretty shady.

122
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,840
Hey, Ottsu, that guy.

123
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:30,560
Yes, we did give the number one,
Mr. Ranking, the bribe.

124
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:32,180
That man, the one from before--

125
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:37,740
With this, there's no doubt our product
will rank high on next week's ranking.

126
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:43,120
How could you possibly know that?!
Who are you people?

127
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:49,260
Let's hear the details, shall we? Yes, yes.

128
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:58,240
Apparently, they routinely bribed the number one so
Mr. Ranking would put their products high on the list.

129
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,640
So that's why those weird
products kept ranking high.

130
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,440
How dare you make us
eat such awful chocolate!

131
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:06,020
We don't make chocolate, though.

132
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,140
Here you go.

133
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,840
I wonder if the TV station
people know about this.

134
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:12,340
I don't think they really know for sure.

135
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:14,320
It would become a matter of trust.

136
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,500
You're going to make it public, of course.

137
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,560
Just making it public
wouldn't be very interesting.

138
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:24,580
Alright, that settles the top three.

139
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,860
Now it's just first and second place.

140
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,013
Harakuro Brewery offers 2 million,

141
00:08:30,063 --> 00:08:32,980
and Warui Brewery offers
1.5 million and a gold bar.

142
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:36,360
It's a tough call which
one to put in first place,

143
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:38,720
but let's go with cash first.

144
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:42,400
Alright, done! Today's ranking
is shaping up nicely, isn't it?

145
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,400
Yeah.

146
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:46,200
Number one Sensei, it's time.

147
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:48,120
Fifteen seconds to air.

148
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:50,600
Alright, let's give it our all today!

149
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:53,280
Five, four, three...

150
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,480
Let's rank anything and everything!

151
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,980
Mr. Ranking!

152
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:07,460
The man who decides the rankings
of everything in the world

153
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,260
That's me.

154
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,500
Deciding the number one spot,

155
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:17,300
today's theme is this.

156
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,180
Sake rankings.

157
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:23,340
So, the sake rankings.

158
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:25,580
And now, the announcement of the number one.

159
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:27,320
This week's number one is

160
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:28,960
from Harakuro Brewery's

161
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:31,100
Aozake Baka Ichidai!

162
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:33,040
Even with its mellow smoothness,

163
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:33,640
it has a refined elegance.

164
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:36,340
It's truly the sake of sakes.

165
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:39,120
Well then, in next week's ranking,

166
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:39,780
let's meet again.

167
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:41,040
All ball

168
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:44,060
I object to that ranking!

169
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:46,860
Aozake Baka Ichidai at number one?

170
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:47,800
Are you kidding me?

171
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,920
Aren't you the one from the other day?

172
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,280
I'll make a better ranking than that!

173
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,000
Hey, hey, wait a minute.

174
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:57,100
Keep the camera rolling!

175
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:00,860
For starters, it's wrong to rank
sake without drinking a single drop!

176
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:09,200
He's guzzling a whole
bottle like it's juice!

177
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:12,480
Interesting!
Let's keep recording just like this!

178
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:18,600
Then, shall we have you rank this one too!

179
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,720
That's more like it!

180
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:33,520
That's all of them.

181
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:38,320
Here, this is my ranking.

182
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:42,675
Oops,

183
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:46,320
this turned out completely
different from Mr. Ranking's.

184
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:49,760
This is total nonsense.

185
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:52,080
I just lined them up at random.

186
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:54,080
If you have a complaint about these results,

187
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,520
let the customers actually drink them

188
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:59,060
and have them judge which one is right.

189
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:00,700
They're amateurs, you know.

190
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,340
What would amateurs know?

191
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:04,940
Most people who drink sake are amateurs.

192
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,160
But there's no need

193
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:07,940
to worry about it that much.

194
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:09,040
Come on, Gonji.

195
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:09,820
Yeah.

196
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,400
We've got plenty of sake ready for you.

197
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:15,620
Okay, everyone.

198
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:18,880
Drink up and taste them
with your own tongues!

199
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:25,380
Is this the sake that
ranked first in this ranking?

200
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:27,320
This is good!

201
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:29,900
Is this the sake that the
walk-in guy ranked first?

202
00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:34,900
Well then, everyone,

203
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:38,940
please raise the card of whichever
ranking you think is correct.

204
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:39,880
Go ahead.

205
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:43,020
What?

206
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,060
W-what is this?
It's some kind of conspiracy!

207
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:47,080
They're trying to frame me!

208
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,760
Bad timing!

209
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:49,860
Look at that.

210
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:50,560
See?

211
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:55,280
Harakuro Tezukuri, two million.

212
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,380
Warui Tezukuri, one and a half million.

213
00:11:57,380 --> 00:12:00,720
I secretly set up a hidden
camera in your dressing room.

214
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,960
When did he set up something like that?

215
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:06,480
It's a tough call,
but let's go with cash first.

216
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,000
What's going on here?

217
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,620
As you can see.

218
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:14,600
This guy was deciding the rankings
based on the bribes he received.

219
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:15,980
He kept it from us.

220
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:16,800
Fine.

221
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,080
Whoa! Mr. Ranking has run away!

222
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:26,260
Nehahaha! Did you see that?
Justice always wins!

223
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:32,180
What? You want me to
take over as Mr. Ranking?

224
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:35,344
Yes, the other day's
broadcast was a huge hit, so

225
00:12:35,394 --> 00:12:39,660
we'd really like Ryo-san to do Mr. Ranking.

226
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:42,460
That's not a bad offer.

227
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:45,320
The show also wants to
repay its debt to you.

228
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:50,080
Since we've been fooled by Ichii-san and
broadcasting false information all this time.

229
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,760
Well, I suppose I could take it on.

230
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:53,520
Really?

231
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:55,120
But as for the pay...

232
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,280
No way, no way.

233
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:59,280
I absolutely won't allow TV appearances!

234
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,320
Bubu-chan!

235
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:02,500
W-wait a second, please!

236
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:07,160
These people are victims who
were fooled by some shoddy critic.

237
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,040
They're really in trouble.

238
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,000
That's right.

239
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Please, I'm begging you.

240
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:15,720
Appearing on their show would be,
so to speak, a good deed.

241
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:19,720
A good deed Then I suppose I can allow it.

242
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:20,660
Really?

243
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:23,720
But there's no appearance fee.

244
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:26,080
N-no way!

245
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:27,370
It's a good deed, after all.

246
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:30,100
You shouldn't take money
for doing a good deed.

247
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,720
Thank you, thank you.

248
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,840
Ryotsu, do your best.

249
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,980
*Huff, huff.*

250
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:41,380
Ranking Daiō, the Ranking King.

251
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:49,160
Ranking King Kankichi Ryotsu,
the Great King!

252
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:52,420
The man who decides rankings
for everything in the world

253
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:55,840
has descended upon 21st-century Japan.

254
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,160
I am the righteous Ranking King!

255
00:14:00,960 --> 00:14:04,560
Damn it, I'm dressed up like this
and they still won't pay me a fee?

256
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:09,020
The theme for the commemorative
first session is retort curry.

257
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:12,380
Now, let's have it decided!

258
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,260
Ranking King!

259
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:19,380
Whoa, look at Ryotsu's incredible eating!

260
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:24,380
Incredibly, he's devoured
ten plates of curry in no time!

261
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:25,940
No, not yet!

262
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:29,140
My motto is to eat them
all before ranking them.

263
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:31,040
Keep bringing them out!

264
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,800
And now, the announcement.

265
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:37,120
This is the curry ranking I put together!

266
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:38,780
Ooh!

267
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,860
I tested every one with my own tongue!

268
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,660
Anyone who has a complaint, bring it on!

269
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:44,740
Ooh!

270
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:48,120
Wow, Ryo-san, that was amazing.

271
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:50,980
So, about next week's ranking...

272
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:53,420
For now, let's focus on food.

273
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,080
Why is that?

274
00:14:55,460 --> 00:14:58,100
Because it's what viewers
are most familiar with.

275
00:14:59,020 --> 00:14:59,420
I see.

276
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:02,200
Sweet Bread Ranking!

277
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:04,280
Bottled Water Ranking

278
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,660
Convenience Store Dessert Ranking

279
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:09,420
Ryo-Approved Ranking King

280
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:11,320
Don't miss it!

281
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:14,560
Senpai, your show's getting amazing reviews.

282
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:18,380
I hear the product Ryo-chan put at
number one is selling like crazy.

283
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:19,800
Is that so?

284
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,760
Aren't you happy about it, Ryo-san?

285
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,240
Of course I'm not happy!

286
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:25,280
No matter how good the show's reviews are,

287
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:27,560
not a single yen comes to me!

288
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,680
Right.

289
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,220
At most, it's my steamed buns that sell.

290
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,000
Cleared it!

291
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,140
Then how about bath salts next?

292
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:37,740
Bath salts?

293
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:42,740
I hear Komachi and the others are arguing over
what bath salts to put in the women's dorm bath.

294
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:46,540
Well, a bath every now
and then isn't so bad.

295
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:51,820
Excuse me, you're Dr. Ryotsu, aren't you?

296
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:53,120
That's right.

297
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:55,200
Please, do accept this.

298
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,960
What, manju again?

299
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,720
Please, do check what's inside.

300
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:03,931
Well, I can't refuse.

301
00:16:03,981 --> 00:16:07,500
Is it really okay to get this much manju?

302
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:13,356
You can never get tired of manju,
no matter how much you eat.

303
00:16:13,406 --> 00:16:14,840
Yeah, this is the one.

304
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:16,880
I'm honored that you're pleased.

305
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:21,740
By the way, which company are you from?
Curry? Or sweet bread?

306
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:22,820
It's bath salts.

307
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:26,200
Bath salts? That's for next week's taping.

308
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,840
So this isn't a thank-you, it's a bribe!

309
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,780
No, no, I can't accept something like this!

310
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:36,480
I have absolute confidence
in my company's products.

311
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:40,380
If they're fairly evaluated,
there's no doubt they'll take first place.

312
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,600
Is that so?

313
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,660
Please, do accept it without any worry.

314
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:47,520
If it takes first place on the show,
sales will shoot up.

315
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:50,440
So I thought I'd hand over my thanks early.

316
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,920
It's, so to speak, a thank-you in advance.

317
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:54,600
A thank-you in advance

318
00:16:56,200 --> 00:17:01,220
Then I'll take it home. Not that I'm the
kind of petty person who'd hold a grudge.

319
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:07,380
I'll gratefully accept it. By the way,
our company's product is Soda Splash.

320
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:13,940
Black. Got it, Soda Splash Black.
Alright, now for the last bath salt.

321
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:18,540
It's Soda Splash Black. This one

322
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,620
It's slimy and unpleasant.

323
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,680
Whoops.

324
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,840
This is wonderful.

325
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:26,940
Wonderful.

326
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:30,800
Pitch-black water that
changes the image of the bath.

327
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,760
A refreshing, fizzy feel on the skin.

328
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:37,180
The number one, no question, is this one.

329
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:40,100
It's the Soda Splash Black,
the under-the-table bribe.

330
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,960
Good work.

331
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:46,400
But I never expected that
one to take first place.

332
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,460
All I did was say that good things are good.

333
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:50,820
It was truly a groundbreaking bath salt.

334
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:54,180
From now on, that might become
the standard for bath salts.

335
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:57,400
Never mind that.
What are we doing for next week's ranking?

336
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,520
How about refrigerators, for instance?

337
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,020
Refrigerators

338
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:04,060
Hello, is this Kanzen Denki?

339
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:07,600
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu, the Ranking King.

340
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:11,940
Actually, we've decided to feature
refrigerators in next week's ranking.

341
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:14,280
No, that's all I wanted to talk about.

342
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:17,620
By the way,
do you know about advance thank-you gifts?

343
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:20,040
Well, think it over.

344
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:25,960
Ryotsu-sensei

345
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:27,240
Sensei

346
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:30,960
It's Kandenden Electric?

347
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:32,560
Yes,

348
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:36,600
I'm in charge of Sabui-kun,
Kandenden Electric's new refrigerator.

349
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:40,860
Today I've brought sweets
as an advance thank-you gift.

350
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:42,120
You shouldn't have.

351
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:45,940
Koban senbei! How auspicious.

352
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:51,320
How did you know koban
senbei is my favorite?

353
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,398
Well, as they say,
a snake knows the way of snakes.

354
00:18:53,448 --> 00:18:56,560
This year's the year of the snake. Say
"tsū," and I'll answer "ka"!

355
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:59,440
Please look after Sabui-kun.

356
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:02,520
Leave it to me. Sabui-kun, right?

357
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:06,620
This week's number one is
Kandenden Electric's Sabui-kun!

358
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:08,100
That's the one.

359
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,720
Justice wins!

360
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:13,060
At this rate, we'll make a fortune!

361
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,500
There, Ryotsu's all wrapped up.

362
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:19,460
What's wrong with you two?

363
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:23,700
My husband recommended that bath salt,
so I bought it.

364
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:24,900
And then...

365
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:27,860
What's with that Soda Splash Black, anyway?

366
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:29,400
Isn't it just creepy?

367
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:30,900
You don't get it, do you.

368
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:31,920
What do you mean?

369
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,920
When cola first came to Japan,

370
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,740
90% of Japanese said it tasted awful!

371
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:37,820
And now look.

372
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:40,760
Now there isn't a single
person who says that!

373
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:43,640
That's a totally different story.

374
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:45,900
Ryotsu-sensei.

375
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:48,000
It's about that bitter...
tea product, though.

376
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:51,080
Let's talk about that over there.

377
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:51,680
Yes.

378
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,100
We're not finished talking, you know.

379
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,320
I'll hear it later.

380
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:58,260
Hello.

381
00:19:58,260 --> 00:20:00,820
Honestly, Ryo-chan.

382
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:04,120
Lately we've had a lot of customers like that,
haven't we?

383
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,460
For Ryo-chan?

384
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,860
They seem to have brought something, though.

385
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:08,800
This is...

386
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:11,380
This might be...

387
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,400
Nigai Sei-chan and
Degarashi-en both hit 2 million

388
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:19,840
Degarashi-en is number one.

389
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:21,680
Because the representative was a beauty.

390
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:23,520
Ryotsu-sensei, it's time.

391
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,380
Coming now.

392
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:29,820
Senpai,

393
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,520
it's Nakagawa.

394
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:34,520
Senpai, I have something to tell you.

395
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:36,520
We're about to go live. Do it after.

396
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:39,280
Senpai, you're receiving

397
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:40,420
about that bribe.

398
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,280
What are you talking about?

399
00:20:44,980 --> 00:20:46,540
I'd never take a bribe.

400
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:49,760
But...

401
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:51,640
Don't say such reckless things.

402
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:52,220
But

403
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:53,000
Professor Ryotsu

404
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,280
Right?

405
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:58,360
I'm the Ranking King of justice, after all.

406
00:20:58,360 --> 00:20:59,520
Let's keep it fair, let's keep it fair.

407
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:02,000
So persuading him was hopeless after all.

408
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:07,420
Ryotsu, representative of the Ranking King.

409
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:11,820
The man who decides rankings
for everything in the world

410
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:14,860
has descended upon 21st-century Japan.

411
00:21:15,360 --> 00:21:17,800
I am the Ranking King of justice!

412
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,320
Now, today's theme is Japanese tea!

413
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:23,760
Hold on a second!

414
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:27,860
Who the hell are you?

415
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:31,460
Let me play you something.

416
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:31,920
Senpai.

417
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:33,340
Nakagawa, is it?

418
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:33,960
What?

419
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,080
That's Kei-chan's voice.

420
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:38,220
It's the conversation
with Senpai from earlier.

421
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:41,120
About the bribes you're receiving, Senpai...

422
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:42,180
A bribe?

423
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:43,440
That's Ryotsu, isn't it?

424
00:21:43,940 --> 00:21:46,160
I knew he'd slip up eventually,

425
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:47,620
so I've been keeping a close watch on him.

426
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,640
Who are you?!

427
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:52,960
It's me!

428
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:54,800
Hey, you!

429
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:58,247
That's right, the one who was
once banished from this show,

430
00:21:58,297 --> 00:21:59,560
the Ranking Decider!

431
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,880
What do you want now, you bastard!

432
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:02,920
W-wait, wait, hey!

433
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:03,740
Haa!

434
00:22:03,980 --> 00:22:05,900
It's interesting! Let it continue!

435
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:06,940
H-huh? What?

436
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:09,800
Ha let me show you something interesting!

437
00:22:13,820 --> 00:22:16,720
Bitter Seicha and Degarashi-E
brought in two million

438
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,860
Because the rep was a beauty.

439
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:24,580
After all, you're doing the same thing I am!

440
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:28,380
N-no! This is some kind of mistake!

441
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:31,880
It's a conspiracy! It's a fraud!

442
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:33,340
Senpai!

443
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:34,920
Ryo-chan!

444
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:35,860
Don't look!

445
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:43,240
Listen! Make them stop!

446
00:23:02,140 --> 00:23:05,480
You bastard! You've wrecked my show!

447
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,820
It was originally my show!

448
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:08,540
What's your problem!

449
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:08,740
Meow!

450
00:23:10,380 --> 00:23:10,840
Ryo!

451
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:12,200
Aisha!

452
00:23:13,500 --> 00:23:14,060
Eesha!

453
00:23:38,540 --> 00:23:43,320
Hey, Reiko-san, this ranking
magazine is super popular right now.

454
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:46,440
Those things are never reliable,
not one of them.

455
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:49,300
But this magazine is actually trustworthy,
you know.

456
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:55,600
Because Ryo Tsukankichi tops
the ranking of untrustworthy men!

457
00:23:58,380 --> 00:24:02,900
Damn it, I hate rankings so much!

458
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:20,540
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out,

459
00:24:21,820 --> 00:24:27,200
walking while looking back,
my hand held by Mom.

460
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:34,420
That mysterious feeling I had back then,

461
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:39,620
so I walked along the
tiles of the arcade street,

462
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:45,400
stepping only on the black ones.

463
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:53,520
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

464
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:57,680
Politicians with their self-important faces

465
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:00,980
and the blue-eyed-shadowed
aunties who look down on us,

466
00:25:00,980 --> 00:25:06,600
try turning that corner over there.

467
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:11,820
You'll be able to meet everyone, everyone.

468
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:19,860
That place is Kameari, well, surely Kameari.

469
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:24,980
Everyone, come on over to our town!

470
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:26,560
Thank you.

471
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,800
What? A magic kettle?

472
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:34,800
Yes, I'm the magic kettle, you see.

473
00:25:34,800 --> 00:25:37,020
What exactly can a magic kettle do?

474
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:38,920
I'll double whatever money you put in.

475
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:40,600
Yay! Now I'm rolling in money!

476
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:44,260
Dang it, why do I only have 5
yen on me at a time like this?

477
00:25:44,700 --> 00:25:47,460
Next time, the magic kettle. See you then!

478
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:01,240
Yay!

